    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nWhen mini.files is launched, it seems like a good idea to use mini.clue, especially with potentially many bookmarks. After adding `MiniClue.ensure_buf_triggers(buf_id)` to an autocmd `MiniFilesBufferCreate`, `'` in mini.files has Neovim suggestions like `' | Line before jump`, overriding mappings for mini.files (i.e. not possible to use bookmark feature anywhere). \r\n\r\nHow to have bookmark clues e.g. `'a`, `'b`, `'c`? and some mappings beginning with `g` in mini.files?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When mini.files is launched, it seems like a good idea to use mini.clue, especially with potentially many bookmarks. After adding <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniClue.ensure_buf_triggers(buf_id)</code> to an autocmd <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesBufferCreate</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> in mini.files has Neovim suggestions like <code class=\"notranslate\">' | Line before jump</code>, overriding mappings for mini.files (i.e. not possible to use bookmark feature anywhere).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How to have bookmark clues e.g. <code class=\"notranslate\">'a</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">'b</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">'c</code>? and some mappings beginning with <code class=\"notranslate\">g</code> in mini.files?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nWhen mini.files is launched, it seems like a good idea to use mini.clue, especially with potentially many bookmarks. After adding MiniClue.ensure_buf_triggers(buf_id) to an autocmd MiniFilesBufferCreate, ' in mini.files has Neovim suggestions like ' | Line before jump, overriding mappings for mini.files (i.e. not possible to use bookmark feature anywhere).\nHow to have bookmark clues e.g. 'a, 'b, 'c? and some mappings beginning with g in mini.files?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
