            "reply_data": [
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "The main problem is that triggers in 'mini.clue' are [implemented as buffer-local mappings](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/9459d7f41ae77d909579dab0aea2bdd3210fac9f/doc/mini-clue.txt#L49-L50). This conflicts with 'mini.files' buffer local mapping for `'` to navigate to the bookmark. As far as I can understand right now, it can only be one (act as 'mini.clue' trigger and show clues) or the other (act as 'mini.files' \"ask user to press a single character and go to that bookmark\").\r\n\r\nSo yeah, 'mini.clue' is a bit special here.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The main problem is that triggers in 'mini.clue' are <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/9459d7f41ae77d909579dab0aea2bdd3210fac9f/doc/mini-clue.txt#L49-L50\">implemented as buffer-local mappings</a>. This conflicts with 'mini.files' buffer local mapping for <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> to navigate to the bookmark. As far as I can understand right now, it can only be one (act as 'mini.clue' trigger and show clues) or the other (act as 'mini.files' \"ask user to press a single character and go to that bookmark\").</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So yeah, 'mini.clue' is a bit special here.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "The main problem is that triggers in 'mini.clue' are implemented as buffer-local mappings. This conflicts with 'mini.files' buffer local mapping for ' to navigate to the bookmark. As far as I can understand right now, it can only be one (act as 'mini.clue' trigger and show clues) or the other (act as 'mini.files' \"ask user to press a single character and go to that bookmark\").\nSo yeah, 'mini.clue' is a bit special here.",
